-- The ties of the three product terms of \cref{lem:qthree} on every side of the three blocks: each has its one member,
-- or its two sides are apart, by the characters of the blocks. The members are identities of masses, also below \(y=1\)
-- and at the self-dual point \(y=1\).
lemma lem:qblocks [three terms on three blocks: the ties on every side]
  (pair): N, tau, sigma, c, a, b, s, t, zB in NN>=1, y, pN, ptau, psig, pc, pa, pb, ps, pt in QQ>0, pN + 1 = y^(2 * N), ptau + 1 = y^(2 * tau), psig + 1 = y^(2 * sigma), pc + 1 = y^(2 * c), pa + 1 = y^(2 * a), pb + 1 = y^(2 * b), ps + 1 = y^(2 * s), pt + 1 = y^(2 * t), (N = s + sigma or s = N + sigma or sigma = N + s), (c = a + b or a = c + b or b = c + a), y = N * tau * sigma * c + zB * (a * b * tau * s) + 1, y^(a + b + s + t) * (pN * ptau * psig * pc) = zB * y^(N + sigma + c + t) * (pa * pb * ptau * ps) : (zB = 1, c = s, a = N, b = sigma) or (zB = 1, c = s, a = sigma, b = N)
